  "post": {
    "caption": "Elizabeth Taylor's Italian was just Bulgari. She went to Rome to film Cleopatra and spent many afternoons in Bulgari's shop on Via Condotti, chatting with the jeweler Gianni Bulgari. Taylor later called the shop a big plus of filming in Rome. Her husband Richard Burton joked that the only Italian she knew was Bulgari, and that he introduced her to beer while she introduced him to Bulgari. He gave her jewels for almost any occasion, and she called them her It's Tuesday, I love you jewels, a phrase from her 2002 book, My Love Affair with Jewelry.",
